Ari Juhani Huttunen writes:
>BTW, why is it that the player can kill _every_ monster in nethack? It would
>seem natural that there exist so powerful monsters that they can't be killed
>by the player. 

I totally agree with this!  I think it is silly that the player can kill 
*everything* -- from dragons to Nazgul to even demon lords (!) (the most 
powerful creatures in all of Hell, for cryin' out loud!  Hell!!)  And all
this when one orc with a wand of death could toast any demigod...

>[Tolkien discussion axed.]
>Anyway, I think this would be a welcome addition to the game. It would 
>introduce a new strategy to game playing: running as fast as you can or 
>trying to sneak past this creature.

Making those stealth and invisibility items valuable, and giving speed items 
a new meaning beyond "I can hit you but you can't hit me."  I think that any
addition to the game that will force players to make tradeoffs and strategy
decisions is a good change.

